---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';import {planets} from '../../lib/planets.mjs';
---
<Layout title="Solar System Planet Explorer — Facts & Comparisons" section="Planets"><div class="wrap"><div class="page-intro"><span class="eyebrow">Our cosmic neighborhood</span><h1>Eight worlds.<br/>Endless perspective.</h1><p>From sun-scorched rock to distant ice giants. Explore the planets, then compare the numbers that make each world its own.</p></div><div class="planet-grid">{planets.map((p,i)=><a class="planet-card" href={`/planets/${p.id}/`}><img src={`/images/${p.id}.webp`} alt={`${p.name}, NASA mission imagery`} width="1024" height={p.id === 'saturn' ? 341 : 576} loading="lazy"/><div><span class="eyebrow">0{i+1} / {p.kind}</span><h2>{p.name} ↗</h2><p>{p.tag}</p></div></a>)}</div><section class="section"><h2>Put the planets in perspective</h2><p>Rounded reference values. Diameters are equatorial; orbital periods are Earth days.</p><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Planet</th><th scope="col">Diameter (km)</th><th scope="col">Orbit (days)</th><th scope="col">Distance (AU)</th><th scope="col">Mean temperature (°C)</th></tr></thead><tbody>{planets.map(p=><tr><th scope="row"><a href={`/planets/${p.id}/`}>{p.name}</a></th><td>{p.diameter.toLocaleString('en-US')}</td><td>{p.period.toLocaleString('en-US')}</td><td>{(p.distance/149.5978707).toFixed(2)}</td><td>{p.temp}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div><p class="worked">Reference: <a class="text-link" href="https://nssdc.gsfc.nasa.gov/planetary/factsheet/">NASA Planetary Fact Sheet</a>. Giant-planet temperatures refer to atmospheric levels, not a solid surface.</p></section></div></Layout>
